    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with a condensed roster availability, anchored by **Liam Hicks**, who sits at a 46.06 efficiency score against May. While **Liam Hicks** holds the primary catcher slot, his value is bolstered by a favorable +11% dynamic platoon edge against a right-handed arm. Given the scarcity of high-speed contributors in our system, we are keeping a close watch on **Nasim Nunez** and **Wade Meckler**; should the official lineups confirm them in the top half of their respective orders, their speed-first profiles will force an immediate recalibration of our efficiency floor to prioritize stolen base volume.\n\nThe bench remains heavy with core talent like **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, and **Luis Robert Jr.**, all of whom are currently inactive due to today\u2019s league-wide off-day. **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, and **Jordan Westburg** are prepared for upcoming series, but their projected efficiency remains dormant until the next active cycle. We continue to monitor the development paths of **Jacob Wilson** and **Henry Bolte** as secondary options should **Heliot Ramos** or **Coby Mayo** see a dip in playing time due to shifting defensive alignments. With the current absence of high-scoring active contributors like **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Drake Baldwin**, and **Sam Antonacci**, our focus remains on preserving game caps and avoiding exposure to sub-40 efficiency ratings until the remainder of the roster returns to the field.",
